  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Child Protection Compact - Improving the Government of the Philippines&apos; Response to Online Sexual Exploitation of Children and Child Labor</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IJM will scale improvements in protection mechanisms for vulnerable children on a national level, and develop a replicable model for combatting online sexual exploitation of children (OSEC) globally. This program will have short and long term outcomes that will address the critical short term needs of current OSEC and labor trafficking victims, whilst working to build long term improvements in the government response. Leveraging the expertise and footprint of each partner in the formal and informal systems, this project will enhance the Philippines Justice Sector&apos;s work to restrain and deter OSEC perpetrators and protect vulnerable children from exploitation on a national scale.</narrative>
  </description>
